<BaseLayout title="About Acupressure Guide: Our Mission & Your Guide" description="Learn about Acupressure Guide, our mission to make evidence-based acupressure information accessible.">
<article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6"><h1 class="mb-4">About Acupressure Guide</h1><p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">Our mission is to make evidence-based acupressure information accessible to everyone. We bridge the gap between ancient Traditional Chinese Medicine wisdom and modern scientific understanding.</p><img src="/images/about-workspace.png" alt="A traditional Chinese medicine practitioner's workspace with acupuncture tools and reference materials" class="w-full rounded-xl shadow-sm mb-8"><section id="mission" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Our Mission</h2><p class="mb-4">Acupressure Guide was created to provide accurate, practical, and scientifically-informed information about acupressure. We believe that everyone should have access to safe, effective self-care tools that can complement conventional healthcare.</p><p class="mb-4">Every article on this site is written with three principles in mind: accuracy (grounded in both TCM tradition and modern research), practicality (clear, actionable instructions you can use immediately), and safety (clear guidance on contraindications and when to seek professional care).</p></section><section id="author" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Meet the Author</h2><div class="bg-stone-100 dark:bg-stone-800 rounded-lg p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Dr. Chen Wei, TCM Practitioner</h3><p class="mb-3">Dr. Chen Wei is a licensed Traditional Chinese Medicine practitioner with over 15 years of clinical experience. She holds a Doctorate in Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine from the American College of Traditional Chinese Medicine and has completed advanced training in medical acupuncture for pain management.</p><p class="mb-3">Dr. Chen's practice focuses on integrative care, combining TCM modalities (acupuncture, acupressure, herbal medicine, and tuina massage) with evidence-based conventional approaches. She has treated thousands of patients for conditions ranging from chronic pain and digestive disorders to stress and sleep issues.</p><p class="mb-0">She is passionate about teaching self-care techniques like acupressure that empower individuals to take an active role in their health and wellbeing.</p></div></section><section id="editorial" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Editorial Standards</h2><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300"><li>All content is reviewed for accuracy before publication</li><li>Health claims are supported by citations to peer-reviewed research where available</li><li>Traditional uses are clearly distinguished from evidence-based applications</li><li>Safety information includes clear contraindications and medical disclaimers</li><li>Content is updated regularly to reflect new research and best practices</li></ul></section><section id="disclaimer" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Medical Disclaimer</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">The information on Acupressure Guide is for general informational purposes only. It does not constitute medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always seek the advice of your physician or other qualified health provider with any questions you may have regarding a medical condition. Never disregard professional medical advice or delay in seeking it because of something you have read on this site.</p></section></article>
</BaseLayout>
